On May 5, 9:06 am, Cuboidz <Dieter.Be...@gmail.com> wrote:
> 1) How thoroughly do you search each dungeon level before continuing
> to the next? Do you try to discover all secret rooms (including shops
> and vaults)? Also, how many times do you search one spot before
> deciding nothing's there (using "n[number]s")?

I generally explore the whole level. It depends on if i need items or
not - if i'm really set to go then if i find the  downstairs and
there's nothing exciting i can see on the rest of the level with
telepathy then i'll go down. But usually i explore the whole level.
Shops i always find (telepathy helps), vaults i find if i need to buy
protection from a priest still. The max i'll stand searching in one
spot is... well, it depends. Hallways have a tendency to just stop so
i tend to give up early there like maybe 5 searches. If i know a door
has to be on one side of a room, i might search a whole lot there (up
to 20?). In general, as you play more, you'll learn to know where
doors/corridors will go and where they'll end. So you know when to
search and when to give up.

> 2) Is "leveling" a good idea in nethack, e.g. running around until you
> see a monster to kill (to gain experience)?

Generally, no. When you level up, the monsters get tougher. What you
want to do is make it so that your level is in line with your
equipment - if you have good AC and a good weapon, wands, etc then
sure level up. Most people find it effective to keep their XL low in
the beginning so that they don't have to face monsters that are very
tough.

> 3) Do you make the effort of picking up every single item, even if you
> don't need it, in order to sell it in a shop - unless the load would
> burden you, or course? Even more, do you run back for items you left
> because you couldn't carry any more items (for the same purpose of
> selling them)?

Generally, no. I have done this if i really needed the cash for
something, but in general i don't do this. I pick up the items i
need / may want later but leave the rest. You can get cash quicker via
other means (stealing from the shop, identifying gems and selling
them, etc) that selling all the junk you find around the dungeon isn't
really worth it.

